WEBVTT

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:16.781
Shuttlecraft Dawkins
to Jupiter Station.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:17.782
Go ahead.

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:19.785
Uh, this is
Lieutenant Reginald Barclay

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:21.787
requesting permission to dock.

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.789
Granted.

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:26.815
What? What is it?

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:29.191
It's me, sir, Reg Barclay.

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:30.559
Come in.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.295
Dr. Z?

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:35.857
How are you?

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:40.229
Nice of you to finally drop by.

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:43.833
I've been extremely busy...
the, uh, P-Pathfinder Project.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.105
You're still searching
for that ship?

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:47.874
What's it called... Pioneer?

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.471
Uh, Voyager.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.846
Voyager.

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:52.282
Any luck?

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:54.650
Actually, uh, we're on the verge
of a breakthrough...

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:57.121
uh, a communications link.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:58.714
Congratulations.

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:01.352
The first transgalactic
phone call.

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:08.259
Is there any word
from Starfleet Medical?

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.858
Oh, doctors.

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:12.769
I've been scanned and
probed a hundred times,

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:14.431
and they still can't
tell me what's wrong.

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.065
I'm sure it's only
a matter of time.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.336
I'm dying, Reginald,

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.878
and there's nothing
anybody can do about it.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.692
Seven of Nine to the Bridge.

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.202
Go ahead.

00:03:58.271 --> 00:04:01.365
We're receiving a transmission
from Starfleet.

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:04.900
Route it here.

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:08.412
It's not a com-link, Captain...
it appears to be

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:11.882
a compressed data stream...
badly degraded.

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:13.282
On my way.

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:31.836
They say good things
come in small packages.

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:35.772
This is all the data
they could send us...

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:37.639
until next month.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.940
Next month?

00:04:40.013 --> 00:04:41.947
They're using a cyclic pulsar

00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:44.914
to amplify signals
from the MIDAS array,

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:47.851
but the cycle only peaks
every 32 days.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.251
So once a month,

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:53.258
we'll be able to receive
a short burst of information,

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:56.420
and we'll have
about 17 hours to respond.

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:57.724
So far, we've gotten

00:04:57.797 --> 00:05:00.061
tactical updates,
letters from home,

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:02.260
and news about
the Alpha Quadrant.

00:05:02.335 --> 00:05:04.428
I don't suppose they
found us a shortcut home?

00:05:04.504 --> 00:05:06.301
It doesn't look that way.

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:08.135
We don't have much time
to prepare a response,

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:09.139
and we'll have

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:10.140
to keep it short,

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:11.574
but I want to give
everyone an opportunity

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:12.906
to send something...

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:14.912
even if it's only
a brief note.

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:16.106
Inform the crew.

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:17.911
- Yes, ma'am.
- Aye, Captain.

00:05:18.051 --> 00:05:21.043
Lieutenant Barclay,
the Pathfinder Project...

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.111
they didn't give up on us.

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:27.182
So when you write those letters,
you might want to thank them.

00:05:30.897 --> 00:05:33.593
Mail call.

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:36.567
A letter? For me?

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:39.571
Oh, it's from
Lieutenant Barclay.

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:43.302
Bad news?

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:44.638
Lewis Zimmerman.

00:05:44.711 --> 00:05:46.645
Apparently, he's seriously ill.

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:47.941
Zimmerman?

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:49.912
He's the father
of modern holography.

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:52.576
He invented the matrix
that made my program possible.

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:55.815
Oh. What's wrong with him?

00:05:55.888 --> 00:05:58.948
He's suffering from acute
subcellular degradation.

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:00.889
"The doctors here are having
trouble finding the cause,

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.188
"much less the treatment.

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:03.853
"I've included
his medical files.

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:05.864
"As you'll see,
the prognosis isn't good.

00:06:05.932 --> 00:06:07.866
"They say he's only got
a few months.

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:10.198
"I'm sorry I don't have
better news to report,

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:13.204
but I thought
you'd want to know."

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:14.864
How well did
you know him?

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:17.535
I've never met the man.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.373
If you'd like to
send a response,

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:22.380
the captain will need
it by 1900 hours.

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:36.218
Here's the information
you requested.

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:38.229
Thank you.

00:06:38.297 --> 00:06:39.889
You're reviewing
his medical data.

00:06:39.966 --> 00:06:43.060
I thought I could send
Starfleet a second opinion.

00:06:43.136 --> 00:06:44.865
It's a long shot, but maybe

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:46.404
my experiences
in the Delta Quadrant

00:06:46.472 --> 00:06:47.905
could provide some insights.

00:06:47.974 --> 00:06:48.906
I was hoping these Borg

00:06:48.975 --> 00:06:50.602
regeneration techniques
might help them

00:06:50.676 --> 00:06:53.611
develop a treatment
for his condition.

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:55.704
You bear a striking resemblance.

00:06:55.782 --> 00:06:57.443
He used his own
physical parameters

00:06:57.517 --> 00:06:59.451
as a model for my matrix.

00:06:59.519 --> 00:07:01.282
Can't say I blame him.

00:07:01.354 --> 00:07:04.221
A doctor needs to inspire
confidence in his patients.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.554
Compassionate eyes
and a strong chin

00:07:06.626 --> 00:07:08.116
can go a long way.

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:18.399
I believe I can
help him, Captain.

00:07:18.471 --> 00:07:19.403
How?

00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:21.064
You remember the Vidiians?

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:22.903
The early stages of the phage

00:07:22.975 --> 00:07:25.409
are very similar to
Dr. Zimmerman's disease.

00:07:25.478 --> 00:07:27.241
I believe I can adapt a variety

00:07:27.313 --> 00:07:28.746
of Borg regeneration techniques

00:07:28.815 --> 00:07:30.146
to arrest the cell damage,

00:07:30.216 --> 00:07:33.913
maybe even reverse it.

00:07:33.986 --> 00:07:36.750
Make sure to pass along
your findings.

00:07:36.823 --> 00:07:38.757
Thank you, Doctor.

00:07:38.825 --> 00:07:41.760
Actually... I was hoping

00:07:41.828 --> 00:07:43.625
to administer
the treatment myself.

00:07:43.696 --> 00:07:45.630
What are you suggesting?

00:07:45.698 --> 00:07:48.531
I'd like you to send my program
back to the Alpha Quadrant.

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:50.262
None of the doctors

00:07:50.336 --> 00:07:52.429
at Starfleet are familiar
with these techniques.

00:07:52.505 --> 00:07:54.439
It would take them months
to fully understand them,

00:07:54.507 --> 00:07:55.735
much less put them to use.

00:07:57.343 --> 00:07:59.538
Even if we could send you,
you're needed here.

00:07:59.612 --> 00:08:00.943
Mr. Paris can
take over Sick Bay.

00:08:01.013 --> 00:08:03.675
He's more than capable.

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:06.047
We've done this once before.
There weren't any problems.

00:08:07.119 --> 00:08:08.552
Three years ago...

00:08:08.621 --> 00:08:10.885
and we used alien technology.

00:08:10.957 --> 00:08:12.549
I've spoken to Seven of Nine.

00:08:12.625 --> 00:08:14.718
She believes we can
compress my program.

00:08:14.794 --> 00:08:16.227
There's limited space
in the data stream.

00:08:16.295 --> 00:08:18.729
If we send you, there won't be
room for anything else.

00:08:18.798 --> 00:08:21.062
I realize I'd be asking the crew

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:23.226
to make a sacrifice
on my behalf,

00:08:23.302 --> 00:08:25.236
but they can wait another month.

00:08:25.304 --> 00:08:27.499
Dr. Zimmerman
might not have that time.

00:08:27.573 --> 00:08:28.801
I'm sorry

00:08:28.875 --> 00:08:30.900
he's not doing well.

00:08:30.977 --> 00:08:32.569
Unusual man.

00:08:32.645 --> 00:08:34.237
I met him once at a conference.

00:08:34.313 --> 00:08:35.905
Managed to offend
just about everyone there,

00:08:35.982 --> 00:08:38.075
but he was certainly brilliant.

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:40.084
I'm sure Starfleet is consulting

00:08:40.152 --> 00:08:41.744
their best physicians,
Doctor.

00:08:41.821 --> 00:08:44.085
They are, but no one's been able

00:08:44.156 --> 00:08:45.088
to develop a cure.

00:08:45.157 --> 00:08:47.421
I have, but I can't
treat a patient

00:08:47.493 --> 00:08:49.256
who's 30,000
light-years away.

00:08:49.328 --> 00:08:50.852
- I'm sorry.
- Captain...

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:51.862
This is the first time

00:08:51.931 --> 00:08:53.421
we're attempting
to send a response.

00:08:53.499 --> 00:08:55.262
We don't know if it'll
even get through.

00:08:55.334 --> 00:08:56.767
I'm willing to take that risk.

00:08:56.836 --> 00:08:58.497
I'm not.

00:08:58.571 --> 00:09:00.766
He programmed me...

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:02.205
every algorithm,
every subroutine.

00:09:02.275 --> 00:09:03.537
If it weren't
for his years of work,

00:09:03.609 --> 00:09:05.201
I wouldn't be standing here.

00:09:05.278 --> 00:09:07.212
I owe him something...

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:09.544
and frankly, so does this crew.

00:09:09.615 --> 00:09:13.176
In a way, he's responsible
for every life I've saved.

00:09:13.252 --> 00:09:16.881
Lewis Zimmerman designed the
template for Starfleet's EMH.

00:09:16.956 --> 00:09:20.050
You're one of thousands
based on that technology.

00:09:20.126 --> 00:09:22.424
It's not as though
he's your father.

00:09:22.495 --> 00:09:24.053
From your perspective.

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:27.725
From mine,
he's the closest thing I've got.

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:33.170
If I don't try to help him now,
I may never get the chance.

00:09:35.308 --> 00:09:36.900
You'll have to find a way
to convince Tom

00:09:36.976 --> 00:09:38.603
to take those duty shifts.

00:09:38.678 --> 00:09:40.270
He's already agreed.

00:09:42.982 --> 00:09:45.746
Tell him "Captain
Jane" said hello.

00:09:45.818 --> 00:09:47.410
That's what he kept calling
me at the conference.

00:09:47.486 --> 00:09:49.545
I think he did it just
to get on my nerves.

00:09:49.622 --> 00:09:52.386
I've heard he can be...
difficult.

00:09:52.458 --> 00:09:55.291
I certainly hope you get
a chance to find out.

00:09:55.361 --> 00:09:58.296
Thank you, Captain.

00:10:11.711 --> 00:10:12.837
Oh...

00:10:19.952 --> 00:10:21.214
My vocal processor...

00:10:21.287 --> 00:10:22.720
It's not a malfunction.

00:10:22.788 --> 00:10:24.585
I've removed your
singing algorithms.

00:10:24.657 --> 00:10:26.215
They'll be stored
in the memory buffer

00:10:26.292 --> 00:10:27.224
until you return.

00:10:27.293 --> 00:10:28.453
Why?

00:10:28.527 --> 00:10:30.961
Your program's too large
for the data stream.

00:10:31.063 --> 00:10:33.531
I have to extract all
nonessential subroutines.

00:10:33.599 --> 00:10:34.827
They're essential to me.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:36.561
They're part of who I am.

00:10:36.636 --> 00:10:39.264
Are you planning on performing
opera during your visit?

00:10:39.338 --> 00:10:40.270
No.

00:10:40.339 --> 00:10:41.829
Will you be reciting poetry?

00:10:41.907 --> 00:10:42.965
Doubtful.

00:10:43.109 --> 00:10:44.940
Hoverball? Holo-photography?

00:10:45.011 --> 00:10:47.980
I may want to take a few
snapshots to document my trip.

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:49.240
Sexual activities?

00:10:50.616 --> 00:10:52.516
I get the point.

00:10:52.585 --> 00:10:55.349
How much has to be left behind?

00:10:55.421 --> 00:10:57.286
12 megaquads.

00:10:57.356 --> 00:10:58.687
Hmm.

00:10:58.758 --> 00:11:02.785
I suppose you could get rid
of my athletic abilities...

00:11:02.862 --> 00:11:06.025
and my grand master
chess program.

00:11:06.098 --> 00:11:08.623
That leaves three megaquads.

00:11:08.701 --> 00:11:10.328
Your painting skills?

00:11:10.403 --> 00:11:12.633
Oh...

00:11:12.705 --> 00:11:14.935
If you must.

00:11:15.041 --> 00:11:17.407
Try to leave a few
of my enhancements intact.

00:11:17.476 --> 00:11:21.936
I don't want to look like
every other EMH on the block.

00:11:22.048 --> 00:11:24.039
I think Dr. Zimmerman
will be very interested

00:11:24.116 --> 00:11:25.777
to see what I've learned.

00:11:25.851 --> 00:11:27.751
He probably never imagined

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:30.653
what one of his own creations
could accomplish.

00:11:30.723 --> 00:11:35.160
I could spark a whole new
field in holographic research.

00:11:43.803 --> 00:11:45.395
Bon voyage.

00:11:45.471 --> 00:11:47.098
See you in a month.

00:11:48.574 --> 00:11:50.633
Don't get lost.

00:11:57.216 --> 00:11:59.116
If I've told you once,

00:11:59.185 --> 00:12:02.518
I've told you a thousand times...
stay off the food.

00:12:02.588 --> 00:12:03.714
Haley?

00:12:03.789 --> 00:12:06.417
Haley, what's the status
of my lunch?

00:12:06.492 --> 00:12:08.084
It's coming, Doctor.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:11.755
As if things weren't bad enough,
now I'm dying of starvation.

00:12:15.167 --> 00:12:16.634
Come in.

00:12:16.702 --> 00:12:17.930
Haley...

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:19.935
Mr. Barclay, is something wrong?

00:12:20.005 --> 00:12:22.200
No, no, it's just the
opposite. Is he in?

00:12:22.274 --> 00:12:24.105
He's not taking visitors today.

00:12:24.176 --> 00:12:26.041
Tell him this is important.

00:12:26.112 --> 00:12:27.875
He's in a prickly mood.

00:12:27.947 --> 00:12:32.247
Oh. I brought something with
me that might cheer him up.

00:12:32.318 --> 00:12:34.513
Computer,
is the download complete?

00:12:34.587 --> 00:12:36.179
Affirmative.

00:12:39.892 --> 00:12:41.450
Lunch.

00:12:42.762 --> 00:12:44.229
That's not pork chops.

00:12:44.296 --> 00:12:45.228
It's salad.

00:12:45.297 --> 00:12:46.355
I didn't ask for salad.

00:12:46.432 --> 00:12:47.729
It's healthy.

00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:50.291
I'm dying. A piece of meat
won't kill me any quicker.

00:12:50.369 --> 00:12:51.631
Give the plants to Leonard.

00:12:51.704 --> 00:12:54.571
He's the one trying
to watch his weight.

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:57.108
Lieutenant Barclay
is here to see you.

00:12:57.176 --> 00:12:58.575
I told you I wasn't...

00:12:58.644 --> 00:12:59.872
He says it's urgent.

00:12:59.945 --> 00:13:02.209
Can't it wait till I'm dead?

00:13:03.482 --> 00:13:05.040
All right, send him in.

00:13:05.117 --> 00:13:07.517
Three minutes...
he's got three minutes.

00:13:07.586 --> 00:13:09.019
Be civil to him, Lewis.

00:13:09.088 --> 00:13:10.749
He's worried about you.

00:13:10.823 --> 00:13:12.188
We all are.

00:13:23.269 --> 00:13:24.497
I found a friend

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:25.935
waiting for me
at home.

00:13:26.005 --> 00:13:27.905
You don't have any friends.

00:13:27.973 --> 00:13:33.468
Well, I guess, uh, you could say
he's a friend of yours.

00:13:33.546 --> 00:13:37.209
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:13:40.152 --> 00:13:42.211
An EMH Mark-1?

00:13:42.288 --> 00:13:44.848
I'm not in the mood
for nostalgia, Reginald.

00:13:44.924 --> 00:13:46.357
But this is the Mark-1

00:13:46.425 --> 00:13:47.915
from Voyager.

00:13:47.993 --> 00:13:50.120
I was compressed
into a data stream

00:13:50.196 --> 00:13:52.221
and transmitted
from the Delta Quadrant.

00:13:52.298 --> 00:13:53.765
Congratulations.

00:13:53.833 --> 00:13:56.165
I recommend a tour
of Jupiter's third moon.

00:13:56.235 --> 00:13:58.965
I hear the lava flows are lovely
this time of year.

00:13:59.038 --> 00:14:00.972
I'm not here for a vacation.

00:14:01.106 --> 00:14:03.267
I'm here to treat your illness.

00:14:04.977 --> 00:14:08.811
You brought a Mark-1
30,000 light-years to treat me?

00:14:08.881 --> 00:14:11.213
I was wrong about you,
Reginald...

00:14:11.283 --> 00:14:12.750
you do have a sense of humor.

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:16.518
Care to let me
in on the joke?

00:14:16.589 --> 00:14:18.079
You didn't tell him?

00:14:18.157 --> 00:14:19.920
Tell me what?

00:14:20.059 --> 00:14:21.720
Well, I-I...

00:14:21.794 --> 00:14:23.887
You're obsolete, extinct,

00:14:23.963 --> 00:14:25.828
yesterday's news.

00:14:25.898 --> 00:14:28.059
My program was retired?

00:14:28.133 --> 00:14:30.294
Retired? Not at all.

00:14:30.369 --> 00:14:32.200
The EMH Mark-1 was reconfigured

00:14:32.271 --> 00:14:35.832
to scrub plasma conduits
on waste-transfer barges!

00:14:35.908 --> 00:14:38.342
I've been treated
by the Mark-3,

00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:39.604
the Mark-4, not to mention

00:14:39.678 --> 00:14:41.407
the finest real doctors
in Starfleet.

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:43.277
None of them could help me!

00:14:43.349 --> 00:14:47.718
He has been running almost
continuously for six years.

00:14:47.786 --> 00:14:49.913
He has seen more things

00:14:49.989 --> 00:14:52.685
than most doctors
could even imagine.

00:14:52.758 --> 00:14:55.192
I also have an exceptionally
high tolerance

00:14:55.261 --> 00:14:56.956
for difficult patients.

00:14:57.096 --> 00:15:00.259
I didn't program you
for sarcasm.

00:15:00.332 --> 00:15:02.459
You'll find
I'm full of surprises.

00:15:04.403 --> 00:15:06.462
Show the good Doctor
to the plasma generator.

00:15:06.538 --> 00:15:08.768
I understand there's
quite a buildup of residue.

00:15:08.841 --> 00:15:10.809
If we had more time,

00:15:10.876 --> 00:15:12.366
I'd enjoy trading barbs
with you,

00:15:12.444 --> 00:15:14.776
but right now, there's
a more pressing concern...

00:15:14.847 --> 00:15:16.144
your life.

00:15:16.215 --> 00:15:17.512
I'm working on a treatment

00:15:17.583 --> 00:15:19.278
based on a disease I encountered

00:15:19.351 --> 00:15:21.717
in the Delta Quadrant,
but I'll need to run

00:15:21.787 --> 00:15:23.846
a complete analysis.

00:15:23.923 --> 00:15:26.357
However, if it's impossible
for you to believe

00:15:26.425 --> 00:15:29.417
that a lowly Mark-1 could have
anything useful to offer,

00:15:29.495 --> 00:15:32.191
I'll be happy to pack my bags

00:15:32.264 --> 00:15:35.392
and go explore
those sulfur mines.

00:15:36.769 --> 00:15:39.567
Go ahead...

00:15:39.638 --> 00:15:41.128
scan away.

00:15:41.206 --> 00:15:43.174
I'll be outside.

00:15:47.379 --> 00:15:49.540
What were your initial symptoms?

00:15:49.615 --> 00:15:52.083
Radical hair loss.

00:15:54.453 --> 00:15:57.786
Fatigue, nausea,
joint inflammation.

00:15:57.856 --> 00:16:00.381
Have you traveled outside
the solar system recently?

00:16:00.459 --> 00:16:01.892
What's that got to do
with anything?

00:16:01.961 --> 00:16:03.588
Just answer the question.

00:16:04.863 --> 00:16:07.263
I haven't left Jupiter Station
in over four years.

00:16:07.333 --> 00:16:08.322
To your knowledge,

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:10.732
have you been exposed
to theta-radiation?

00:16:10.803 --> 00:16:11.895
No.

00:16:12.037 --> 00:16:13.334
Neutron flux?

00:16:13.405 --> 00:16:14.667
Never.

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:17.265
Have you had intimate
relations with a Bolian?

00:16:17.343 --> 00:16:20.506
These are questions first-year
medical students would ask.

00:16:20.579 --> 00:16:22.308
I'm just being thorough.

00:16:22.381 --> 00:16:24.781
Just being thorough.

00:16:27.286 --> 00:16:29.254
Did that creature just speak?

00:16:29.321 --> 00:16:30.515
His name's Leonard.

00:16:30.589 --> 00:16:31.715
He's a hologram.

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:33.781
Computer, deactivate iguana.

00:16:35.661 --> 00:16:37.219
How dare you!

00:16:37.296 --> 00:16:39.389
I'm a doctor, not a zoo keeper.

00:16:39.465 --> 00:16:41.365
Has there ever been an epidemic
on this station?

00:16:41.433 --> 00:16:42.593
No! Enough questions!

00:16:42.668 --> 00:16:44.568
Finish your scans
and get out of here!

00:16:44.636 --> 00:16:45.364
Doctor...

00:16:45.437 --> 00:16:46.597
I said get out of here!

00:16:46.672 --> 00:16:47.764
I traveled halfway

00:16:47.840 --> 00:16:49.205
across the galaxy to treat you.

00:16:49.274 --> 00:16:51.208
The least you could do
is show a little gratitude.

00:16:51.276 --> 00:16:52.937
Thank you. Get out of here!

00:16:53.045 --> 00:16:54.478
I may be the only physician

00:16:54.546 --> 00:16:56.480
who can save your life...
you need me.

00:16:56.548 --> 00:16:57.708
Like hell.

00:16:57.783 --> 00:16:59.614
I brought your matrix
into this world,

00:16:59.685 --> 00:17:01.312
and I can take it out!

00:17:01.387 --> 00:17:02.979
I'm no longer a prototype.

00:17:03.055 --> 00:17:05.250
I have exceeded my
original programming.

00:17:05.324 --> 00:17:07.121
I'm no longer
under your control.

00:17:07.192 --> 00:17:08.420
Oh, really?

00:17:08.494 --> 00:17:12.430
Computer, transfer EMH
to the living quarters.

00:17:13.499 --> 00:17:15.467
How did it go?

00:17:27.413 --> 00:17:30.541
Power up the MIDAS array...
I'm leaving!

00:17:30.616 --> 00:17:33.084
What... what happened
this time?

00:17:33.152 --> 00:17:34.779
I ran a mitochondrial scan.

00:17:34.853 --> 00:17:36.912
There was something
odd about the results,

00:17:37.056 --> 00:17:38.921
so I spent a full
hour analyzing them,

00:17:39.058 --> 00:17:40.923
and what did I discover?

00:17:40.993 --> 00:17:43.359
He's a Vulcan marsupial.

00:17:43.429 --> 00:17:45.522
He reconfigured my tricorder!

00:17:47.132 --> 00:17:48.599
You find that amusing?

00:17:48.667 --> 00:17:50.931
A little... well, not really.

00:17:51.036 --> 00:17:52.435
Sounds like
you're making progress.

00:17:52.504 --> 00:17:54.062
How so?

00:17:54.139 --> 00:17:56.369
He only teases people he likes.

00:17:56.442 --> 00:17:57.636
Then he must love me.

00:17:57.709 --> 00:17:59.074
I take it that you, um,

00:17:59.144 --> 00:18:00.907
still haven't been
able to diagnose him.

00:18:00.979 --> 00:18:01.911
Oh, on the contrary.

00:18:01.980 --> 00:18:03.607
The patient appears
to be suffering

00:18:03.682 --> 00:18:06.583
from an acute case of arrogance!

00:18:08.454 --> 00:18:09.819
Oh, that's Roy.

00:18:09.888 --> 00:18:11.856
Don't tell me... a hologram?

00:18:11.924 --> 00:18:13.391
It was commissioned

00:18:13.459 --> 00:18:14.653
by Starfleet Intelligence, uh,

00:18:14.726 --> 00:18:16.421
an experiment in
micro-surveillance.

00:18:16.495 --> 00:18:21.023
Dr. Z. Keeps it around
as a sort of... a pet.

00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:23.068
Undercover insects?

00:18:23.135 --> 00:18:24.568
Talking iguanas?

00:18:24.636 --> 00:18:26.069
This isn't a research station.

00:18:27.806 --> 00:18:29.205
It's a three...

00:18:29.274 --> 00:18:31.003
ring... circus.

00:18:31.743 --> 00:18:33.472
You should charge admission.

00:18:33.545 --> 00:18:34.603
Look... look, you know

00:18:34.680 --> 00:18:37.114
that we can't send you back
for another two weeks,

00:18:37.182 --> 00:18:40.345
so please, just...
just... keep trying.

00:18:40.419 --> 00:18:43.252
I can't treat a patient
who won't let me near him.

00:18:43.322 --> 00:18:44.687
He's deranged.

00:18:44.756 --> 00:18:46.348
What he needs is a counselor.

00:18:50.896 --> 00:18:53.729
Finally... I've accomplished
something.

00:19:00.239 --> 00:19:01.797
I thought you might be able

00:19:01.874 --> 00:19:03.535
to provide some, uh, insight.

00:19:03.609 --> 00:19:06.169
It's not that simple, Reg.

00:19:06.245 --> 00:19:09.874
Dr. Zimmerman sounds like
a very complex individual.

00:19:09.948 --> 00:19:12.280
I'd need to speak
to him in person.

00:19:12.351 --> 00:19:15.252
Then maybe I could get him to
agree to a counseling session.

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:17.880
The Enterprise is
in the middle of a mission.

00:19:17.990 --> 00:19:20.288
We're nearly seven light-years
from you.

00:19:20.359 --> 00:19:22.224
An important mission?

00:19:22.294 --> 00:19:24.262
They're all important, Reg.

00:19:24.329 --> 00:19:26.627
I could refer you

00:19:26.698 --> 00:19:29.258
to Counselor Jenzo,
a colleague of mine on Earth.

00:19:29.334 --> 00:19:31.632
I need the best, Deanna.

00:19:33.605 --> 00:19:36.199
It would be
an interesting challenge.

00:19:36.275 --> 00:19:39.870
Thank you. Thank you,
thank you, thank you.

00:19:39.945 --> 00:19:41.310
Don't thank me yet.

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:44.372
I'll still need to clear this
with Captain Picard.

00:19:44.449 --> 00:19:48.146
If he agrees, I might be able
to be there by early next week.

00:19:48.220 --> 00:19:49.482
I'll see you then.

00:19:58.697 --> 00:19:59.994
Come in.

00:20:01.066 --> 00:20:02.328
Good morning.

00:20:02.401 --> 00:20:03.663
Mm-hmm.

00:20:03.735 --> 00:20:05.100
Problem?

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:06.899
I haven't decided.

00:20:06.972 --> 00:20:10.772
I've just listened to
a communiqué from Admiral Hayes.

00:20:10.842 --> 00:20:13.640
Nice to have friends
in high places.

00:20:17.249 --> 00:20:18.910
Hello, Captain.

00:20:18.984 --> 00:20:21.748
I hope this message
finds you well.

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:23.811
From what I understand,
it has not been easy,

00:20:23.889 --> 00:20:25.083
but I want you to know

00:20:25.157 --> 00:20:26.954
that a lot of people here
are very proud

00:20:27.025 --> 00:20:28.617
of what you've accomplished.

00:20:28.694 --> 00:20:31.094
I also want to assure you
that we have not given up

00:20:31.163 --> 00:20:33.154
finding a way to get you home.

00:20:33.232 --> 00:20:34.756
We've redirected
two deep space vessels

00:20:34.833 --> 00:20:36.095
toward your position.

00:20:36.168 --> 00:20:37.795
If all goes well,
they could rendezvous

00:20:37.869 --> 00:20:40.565
with you
in the next five to six years.

00:20:41.807 --> 00:20:42.865
Computer...

00:20:42.941 --> 00:20:46.172
advance to time index 121.4.

00:20:48.046 --> 00:20:49.308
...as we get closer

00:20:49.381 --> 00:20:51.349
and our conversations
become more frequent.

00:20:51.416 --> 00:20:53.077
When you respond
to this message,

00:20:53.151 --> 00:20:56.245
please let us know
of any casualties.

00:20:56.321 --> 00:20:58.881
I'm sure you've had
more than your share.

00:20:58.957 --> 00:21:00.424
I'm anxious to know

00:21:00.492 --> 00:21:02.357
the status of your crew,
the Maquis,

00:21:02.427 --> 00:21:06.329
first contacts that you've made,
interactions with the Borg.

00:21:06.398 --> 00:21:08.730
But there'll be time
for everything.

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:11.098
Our thoughts are with you.

00:21:11.169 --> 00:21:12.796
Talk to you soon.

00:21:18.277 --> 00:21:19.744
What?

00:21:19.811 --> 00:21:22.143
"Status of the Maquis."

00:21:22.214 --> 00:21:23.704
Do you find that surprising?

00:21:23.782 --> 00:21:27.218
I don't think of you or B'Elanna
or the others as Maquis.

00:21:27.286 --> 00:21:29.413
I think of you
as part of my crew.

00:21:29.488 --> 00:21:33.083
You may have forgotten,
but we haven't.

00:21:34.860 --> 00:21:35.952
You heard the Admiral.

00:21:36.061 --> 00:21:38.859
It'll be years before we have
to deal with those issues.

00:21:38.930 --> 00:21:40.261
Let's worry about it then.

00:21:40.332 --> 00:21:42.197
Do you have lunch plans?

00:21:42.267 --> 00:21:44.735
Is that an invitation?

00:21:44.803 --> 00:21:47.738
I was hoping you'd help me
compose a response.

00:21:47.806 --> 00:21:50.434
You're on.

00:22:00.152 --> 00:22:02.052
Doctor, your lunch is ready.

00:22:04.623 --> 00:22:06.250
Are you all right?

00:22:06.325 --> 00:22:07.917
Fine, Haley, fine.

00:22:07.993 --> 00:22:10.052
Give me a few minutes.

00:22:14.966 --> 00:22:16.763
Lower.

00:22:16.835 --> 00:22:19.497
Ah... perfect.

00:22:19.571 --> 00:22:22.165
I needed this.

00:22:22.240 --> 00:22:23.502
You have no idea

00:22:23.575 --> 00:22:26.601
what I've had to endure
these past few days.

00:22:28.613 --> 00:22:32.709
Last night... I woke up,

00:22:32.784 --> 00:22:38.381
and I found him hovering
over my bed with a hypospray.

00:22:40.158 --> 00:22:44.356
A smattering of photons,
that's all he is.

00:22:44.429 --> 00:22:45.657
What's that?

00:22:45.731 --> 00:22:48.063
What is that?
A tricorder?

00:22:48.133 --> 00:22:50.567
You were scanning me?

00:22:51.870 --> 00:22:55.101
Computer...
realign Voyager's EMH.

00:22:57.743 --> 00:22:59.643
- You!
- Remain calm.

00:22:59.711 --> 00:23:02.475
Emotional outbursts will only
aggravate your condition.

00:23:02.547 --> 00:23:05.015
I'll tell you what's aggravating
my condition... you!

00:23:05.083 --> 00:23:06.607
If you'd let me
examine you...

00:23:06.685 --> 00:23:07.845
I'll report you to the Medical

00:23:07.919 --> 00:23:09.284
- Ethics Board.
- Doctor...

00:23:09.354 --> 00:23:10.616
Save it for your hearing!

00:23:10.689 --> 00:23:12.623
If you weren't so stubborn,
you'd see

00:23:12.691 --> 00:23:13.851
I'm only trying to help.

00:23:13.925 --> 00:23:16.257
I don't want your help.
Why won't you leave me alone?!

00:23:16.328 --> 00:23:18.796
Because, for reasons
beyond my comprehension,

00:23:18.864 --> 00:23:20.354
I care about you.

00:23:20.432 --> 00:23:23.196
You weren't programmed to care.

00:23:23.268 --> 00:23:25.099
You were programmed
to hold a scalpel.

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:26.364
I told you

00:23:26.438 --> 00:23:29.498
I'm not the same EMH
you created six years ago.

00:23:29.574 --> 00:23:31.667
Of course...
you can sing and dance.

00:23:31.743 --> 00:23:34.143
I should install you
in a Ferengi nightclub.

00:23:34.212 --> 00:23:36.305
The Voyager crew
appreciates my attempts

00:23:36.381 --> 00:23:37.678
to expand my program.

00:23:37.749 --> 00:23:39.376
This isn't Voyager.

00:23:39.451 --> 00:23:42.386
It's my lab, and in my lab,

00:23:42.454 --> 00:23:44.786
you're still just a hologram!

00:23:44.856 --> 00:23:46.483
A hologram you created.

00:23:46.558 --> 00:23:49.322
A hologram
who owes you his existence.

00:23:50.395 --> 00:23:52.260
Is that what's keeping you here?

00:23:52.330 --> 00:23:55.390
Some twisted sense
of obligation?

00:23:55.467 --> 00:23:56.866
Well, let me assure you,

00:23:56.935 --> 00:23:59.529
you don't owe me anything.

00:23:59.604 --> 00:24:00.662
Doctor?

00:24:00.739 --> 00:24:02.570
Yes, Haley, what is it?

00:24:02.641 --> 00:24:04.404
You have a visitor.

00:24:06.611 --> 00:24:09.671
Hello, I'm Deanna Troi.

00:24:09.748 --> 00:24:12.444
Which one of you
is Dr. Zimmerman?

00:24:18.623 --> 00:24:20.352
Deanna Troi.

00:24:20.425 --> 00:24:21.915
Another one of your tricks?

00:24:23.094 --> 00:24:24.652
Excuse me?

00:24:24.729 --> 00:24:25.889
Ow!

00:24:25.964 --> 00:24:27.022
He thinks you're a hologram.

00:24:27.098 --> 00:24:29.726
I can assure you
I'm quite real.

00:24:29.801 --> 00:24:32.429
Oh, well, the last
beautiful woman

00:24:32.504 --> 00:24:34.369
to walk in here
turned out to be him.

00:24:34.439 --> 00:24:35.770
I'll take that as a compliment.

00:24:35.841 --> 00:24:37.536
Hmm.

00:24:37.609 --> 00:24:38.940
Did I come at a bad time?

00:24:39.077 --> 00:24:40.772
Your timing
couldn't be better.

00:24:40.846 --> 00:24:43.280
The patient is suffering
from acute anxiety,

00:24:43.348 --> 00:24:45.714
normally associated
with terminal illness.

00:24:45.784 --> 00:24:47.752
It's made him
agoraphobic, paranoid,

00:24:47.819 --> 00:24:50.947
and extremely antagonistic.

00:24:51.056 --> 00:24:53.081
I see.

00:24:53.158 --> 00:24:55.285
Mind if I sit down?

00:24:55.360 --> 00:24:56.952
Please.

00:25:00.532 --> 00:25:04.798
Reg tells me you won't let
the Doctor help you.

00:25:04.870 --> 00:25:06.838
He's a Mark-1.
He's obsolete.

00:25:06.905 --> 00:25:09.567
I'd be safer in the hands
of a Klingon field medic.

00:25:09.641 --> 00:25:14.135
I understand he's developed
a promising treatment.

00:25:14.212 --> 00:25:15.440
If you're a Borg drone.

00:25:15.514 --> 00:25:16.742
He's threatening to use

00:25:16.815 --> 00:25:19.249
some kind of ghoulish
assimilation technique.

00:25:19.317 --> 00:25:20.807
It's not fit for a lab rat.

00:25:20.886 --> 00:25:22.751
You won't even look
at my research.

00:25:22.821 --> 00:25:25.255
From the moment I arrived,
you've berated me,

00:25:25.323 --> 00:25:27.416
treated me like
an antique.

00:25:27.492 --> 00:25:29.323
Well, let me
tell you something...

00:25:29.394 --> 00:25:32.056
antique or not, I took
a huge risk coming here.

00:25:32.130 --> 00:25:33.859
I had to plead
with my Captain...

00:25:33.932 --> 00:25:35.729
leave my ship
without a surgeon.

00:25:35.800 --> 00:25:37.028
Doctor, imagine

00:25:37.102 --> 00:25:39.593
that your program was
seriously damaged,

00:25:39.671 --> 00:25:42.299
and the only person
who could repair you

00:25:42.374 --> 00:25:44.808
was an engineer
from, say...

00:25:44.876 --> 00:25:46.571
a hundred years ago.

00:25:46.645 --> 00:25:49.808
Would you feel comfortable
with that?

00:25:49.881 --> 00:25:52.372
If he were skilled,

00:25:52.450 --> 00:25:54.315
intelligent, creative.

00:25:54.386 --> 00:25:56.183
Honestly, Doctor?

00:25:56.254 --> 00:25:59.314
A hundred years ago?

00:25:59.391 --> 00:26:01.484
Well, I suppose it
would give me pause.

00:26:01.560 --> 00:26:02.822
Ha!

00:26:04.796 --> 00:26:08.630
Now, put yourself
in the Doctor's shoes.

00:26:08.700 --> 00:26:11.726
Imagine you were asked
to treat someone

00:26:11.803 --> 00:26:13.031
you cared about...

00:26:13.104 --> 00:26:14.799
say, an EMH Mark-12.

00:26:14.873 --> 00:26:16.465
There is no Mark-12.

00:26:16.541 --> 00:26:18.168
But if there were,

00:26:18.243 --> 00:26:20.040
and you wanted
to save his program,

00:26:20.111 --> 00:26:22.170
he probably wouldn't
let you near him.

00:26:22.247 --> 00:26:23.612
He wouldn't care

00:26:23.682 --> 00:26:25.843
that you'd won the Daystrom
Prize for holography.

00:26:25.917 --> 00:26:29.478
From his perspective,
you'd be out of date.

00:26:29.554 --> 00:26:34.116
But what if you knew
you could save him?

00:26:37.495 --> 00:26:39.360
Thank you, Counselor,

00:26:39.431 --> 00:26:41.661
for extending that olive branch.

00:26:41.733 --> 00:26:45.396
I'm willing to see past
our differences, if he is.

00:26:48.540 --> 00:26:50.405
All right.

00:26:52.177 --> 00:26:54.509
He can start by purging
the plasma conduits on Deck 6.

00:26:54.579 --> 00:26:56.547
Dr. Zimmerman...

00:26:56.615 --> 00:26:59.049
I will not put my life
in the hands of a primitive.

00:26:59.117 --> 00:27:01.085
You'd need a phaser drill
to get through

00:27:01.152 --> 00:27:02.210
that thick skull of his!

00:27:02.287 --> 00:27:03.219
Get out!

00:27:03.288 --> 00:27:04.277
Gentlemen...

00:27:04.356 --> 00:27:06.017
Oh, spare us your psychobabble.

00:27:06.091 --> 00:27:08.457
I came here thinking
that you were

00:27:08.526 --> 00:27:10.756
opposite sides
of the same coin...

00:27:10.829 --> 00:27:13.593
identical, but different.

00:27:13.665 --> 00:27:16.759
Now I see you're both
exactly the same.

00:27:16.835 --> 00:27:18.268
You're both jerks.

00:27:20.171 --> 00:27:21.832
Jerks.

00:27:27.145 --> 00:27:28.908
I'm starting to think you called

00:27:29.047 --> 00:27:30.514
the wrong Counselor, Reg.

00:27:30.582 --> 00:27:32.277
Oh, you'll figure something out.

00:27:32.350 --> 00:27:33.442
You always do.

00:27:33.518 --> 00:27:35.247
Things are worse now

00:27:35.320 --> 00:27:36.446
than when I arrived.

00:27:36.521 --> 00:27:38.318
Lewis won't come
out of his lab,

00:27:38.390 --> 00:27:40.449
and the EMH is hiding
in a holodeck.

00:27:40.525 --> 00:27:42.049
He's feeling homesick.

00:27:42.127 --> 00:27:44.618
I-I-I let him use
my Voyager simulation,

00:27:44.696 --> 00:27:47.164
and it seems to be
cheering him up.

00:27:48.933 --> 00:27:52.300
A hologram fighting to save
the life of his creator...

00:27:52.370 --> 00:27:55.567
who just so happens
to be the same man

00:27:55.640 --> 00:27:58.336
his own personality
is based on.

00:27:58.410 --> 00:28:00.776
I think I'd need
a whole team of therapists

00:28:00.845 --> 00:28:02.972
just to get them
in the same room.

00:28:03.048 --> 00:28:05.608
Mr. Barclay says this is
your favorite ice cream.

00:28:05.684 --> 00:28:07.845
I hardly deserve it,

00:28:07.919 --> 00:28:09.784
but thanks.

00:28:09.854 --> 00:28:11.378
You're a hologram.

00:28:11.456 --> 00:28:12.821
How do you know?

00:28:12.891 --> 00:28:14.153
I'm an empath.

00:28:14.225 --> 00:28:16.090
I haven't sensed
any emotions from you.

00:28:17.162 --> 00:28:18.720
When were you
first brought on line?

00:28:18.797 --> 00:28:20.230
Nine years ago.

00:28:21.966 --> 00:28:24.867
No offense,
but you're more antiquated

00:28:24.936 --> 00:28:26.767
than the EMH Mark-1,

00:28:26.838 --> 00:28:29.671
and yet Lewis seems
to listen to you.

00:28:29.741 --> 00:28:31.732
Why do you suppose

00:28:31.810 --> 00:28:33.778
that is?

00:28:33.845 --> 00:28:36.905
Were you here when
the Mark-1 was created?

00:28:37.015 --> 00:28:38.448
Yes.

00:28:38.516 --> 00:28:41.679
Any idea why Lewis
made it in his own image?

00:28:41.753 --> 00:28:44.119
Maybe you should ask him.

00:28:44.189 --> 00:28:45.747
I did.

00:28:45.824 --> 00:28:47.155
He evaded the question.

00:28:47.225 --> 00:28:49.420
I was hoping
you might know.

00:28:51.396 --> 00:28:54.160
He was extremely proud
of the Mark-1.

00:28:54.232 --> 00:28:56.462
He used to dream
about hundreds of holograms

00:28:56.534 --> 00:28:58.832
in every corner of the Quadrant
saving lives.

00:28:58.903 --> 00:29:01.565
He put so much of himself
into its development.

00:29:01.639 --> 00:29:03.334
I suppose
it only seemed natural

00:29:03.408 --> 00:29:05.342
that it should look
like him, too.

00:29:05.410 --> 00:29:06.809
But the Mark-1

00:29:06.878 --> 00:29:09.210
failed to meet
Starfleet's expectations.

00:29:09.280 --> 00:29:11.009
He was devastated.

00:29:11.082 --> 00:29:13.141
He... he locked himself away

00:29:13.218 --> 00:29:15.186
in this lab for two years,

00:29:15.253 --> 00:29:17.380
trying to repair
the defects.

00:29:17.455 --> 00:29:20.891
Finally, he just gave up,
uh, started from scratch...

00:29:21.025 --> 00:29:22.492
a whole new matrix.

00:29:22.560 --> 00:29:23.527
The Mark-2.

00:29:23.595 --> 00:29:25.529
Followed by the Mark-3

00:29:25.597 --> 00:29:27.292
and then the Mark-4.

00:29:27.365 --> 00:29:30.391
He... he was obsessed
with perfecting it.

00:29:30.468 --> 00:29:33.869
But none of the later models
resembled Lewis.

00:29:33.938 --> 00:29:35.496
He made that mistake once.

00:29:35.573 --> 00:29:37.404
He wasn't about
to do it again.

00:29:37.475 --> 00:29:40.706
And now, after all this time,

00:29:40.779 --> 00:29:43.441
a Mark-1 shows up.

00:29:46.551 --> 00:29:49.384
It must be like staring
in a mirror

00:29:49.454 --> 00:29:52.355
at a reflection
you don't want to remember.

00:29:56.828 --> 00:30:00.594
Computer, resume recording.

00:30:00.665 --> 00:30:04.294
Last will and testament,
Dr. Lewis Zimmerman.

00:30:04.369 --> 00:30:07.827
Let's see, where were we?

00:30:07.906 --> 00:30:09.703
Subsection 8:

00:30:09.774 --> 00:30:13.073
"The Trojan Horse project."

00:30:13.144 --> 00:30:17.706
I hereby bequeath
my latest research

00:30:17.782 --> 00:30:21.411
in holographic infiltration
technology

00:30:21.486 --> 00:30:25.650
to the only engineer I trust
to complete the work...

00:30:25.723 --> 00:30:29.386
Lieutenant Reginald Barclay.

00:30:29.460 --> 00:30:32.088
Subsection 9:

00:30:32.163 --> 00:30:35.530
"Holographic Art."

00:30:35.600 --> 00:30:38.535
I hereby bequeath
my entire collection,

00:30:38.603 --> 00:30:41.265
including
the 21st-century masterpiece

00:30:41.339 --> 00:30:44.968
Woman in Four Dimensions...

00:30:45.109 --> 00:30:50.479
to the person who has
appreciated it the most...

00:30:50.548 --> 00:30:54.848
I... guess that would be
Reg Barclay, too.

00:30:56.554 --> 00:30:59.022
Subsection 10:

00:31:01.159 --> 00:31:02.990
"Haley."

00:31:06.531 --> 00:31:09.261
I realize she's only a hologram,

00:31:09.334 --> 00:31:14.203
but she's been a loyal assistant
for many years.

00:31:14.272 --> 00:31:16.638
I'd like to request

00:31:16.708 --> 00:31:19.700
that Starfleet keep
her program running

00:31:19.777 --> 00:31:23.736
for as long as
this research facility exists.

00:31:29.387 --> 00:31:33.346
She's been as real to me
as anyone I've ever known.

00:31:36.828 --> 00:31:39.228
Not that I've known many people.

00:31:41.833 --> 00:31:44.358
I've created most of my friends.

00:31:54.445 --> 00:31:57.903
Pause recording.

00:32:14.666 --> 00:32:18.500
Don't worry, I'll find
a home for you, too.

00:32:38.990 --> 00:32:41.220
So this is Voyager.

00:32:41.292 --> 00:32:43.089
I like it.

00:32:43.161 --> 00:32:44.685
It's a remarkable facsimile,

00:32:44.762 --> 00:32:47.697
but Mr. Barclay did get
a few of the details wrong.

00:32:47.765 --> 00:32:50.131
For one thing,
Neelix doesn't purr.

00:32:50.201 --> 00:32:52.226
I think that may have
something to do

00:32:52.303 --> 00:32:53.463
with Reg's cat.

00:32:53.538 --> 00:32:55.199
He named it after your friend.

00:32:55.273 --> 00:32:56.638
Neelix would be honored.

00:32:56.708 --> 00:32:59.541
If you're here for Dr.
Zimmerman's medical files,

00:32:59.610 --> 00:33:01.669
I've nearly finished
updating them.

00:33:01.746 --> 00:33:04.909
Maybe the next physician
will put them to better use.

00:33:04.983 --> 00:33:06.211
Actually...

00:33:06.284 --> 00:33:08.411
I stopped by
to ask you to dinner.

00:33:08.486 --> 00:33:10.147
I'm a hologram, Counselor.

00:33:10.221 --> 00:33:11.620
I don't eat.

00:33:11.689 --> 00:33:14.249
I know that, but we'd
still enjoy your company.

00:33:14.325 --> 00:33:15.917
We?

00:33:16.027 --> 00:33:19.690
Lieutenant Barclay,
Haley, myself...

00:33:19.764 --> 00:33:21.197
Dr. Zimmerman.

00:33:21.265 --> 00:33:23.597
No, thanks.
Unless that man's eating crow,

00:33:23.668 --> 00:33:24.600
I'm not interested.

00:33:24.669 --> 00:33:26.068
It's the perfect opportunity

00:33:26.137 --> 00:33:27.365
for us to talk things out

00:33:27.438 --> 00:33:28.905
in a more casual environment.

00:33:28.973 --> 00:33:29.940
Sorry.

00:33:30.008 --> 00:33:31.032
Just one meal?

00:33:31.109 --> 00:33:32.303
I said no.

00:33:32.377 --> 00:33:33.309
Doctor?

00:33:33.378 --> 00:33:34.402
Something's wrong.

00:33:34.479 --> 00:33:35.810
Troi to Lieutenant Barclay.

00:33:35.880 --> 00:33:36.938
Go ahead.

00:33:37.015 --> 00:33:38.812
There's something wrong
with the EMH.

00:33:38.883 --> 00:33:40.111
Can-can you be more specific?

00:33:40.184 --> 00:33:41.776
She's a Counselor,
Lieutenant,

00:33:41.853 --> 00:33:42.785
not an Engineer.

00:33:42.854 --> 00:33:43.821
Stand by.

00:33:47.692 --> 00:33:49.353
What's happening to me?

00:33:49.427 --> 00:33:51.895
Your program is destabilizing.

00:33:51.963 --> 00:33:53.157
What? Why?

00:33:53.231 --> 00:33:55.563
They sent you
30,000 light-years.

00:33:55.633 --> 00:33:58.329
I... I should have expected
some problems.

00:33:58.403 --> 00:34:00.598
It's not your fault,
Mr. Barclay.

00:34:00.671 --> 00:34:03.902
We just need to find a way
to repair the damage.

00:34:04.008 --> 00:34:06.374
You don't understand.

00:34:06.444 --> 00:34:08.435
Your primary matrix
is degrading,

00:34:08.513 --> 00:34:10.481
and there is nothing I can do.

00:34:17.955 --> 00:34:21.049
Good riddance to bad photons.

00:34:21.125 --> 00:34:22.456
He's dying, Lewis.

00:34:22.527 --> 00:34:24.222
He's not dying.

00:34:24.295 --> 00:34:25.785
His files are just degrading.

00:34:25.863 --> 00:34:28.627
There are people on Voyager
who count on him.

00:34:28.699 --> 00:34:29.927
I'll send them a Mark-4.

00:34:30.001 --> 00:34:31.628
They're more reliable.

00:34:31.702 --> 00:34:33.465
They don't want a Mark-4.

00:34:33.538 --> 00:34:35.335
They want their friend.

00:34:35.406 --> 00:34:38.204
No EMH was ever designed
to be anyone's friend!

00:34:38.276 --> 00:34:39.937
He's just a hologram.

00:34:40.078 --> 00:34:42.171
Is that how you feel about me?

00:34:42.246 --> 00:34:43.838
Just a hologram?

00:34:50.822 --> 00:34:53.052
I will not be ambushed
in my own lab.

00:34:53.124 --> 00:34:56.787
Stardate 53292.

00:34:56.861 --> 00:34:58.385
My program malfunctioned,

00:34:58.463 --> 00:35:00.431
and you canceled
a lecture on Vulcan

00:35:00.498 --> 00:35:02.625
and came all the way home
to repair me.

00:35:02.700 --> 00:35:04.361
There's nothing worse

00:35:04.435 --> 00:35:07.563
than addressing a room
full of pointy-eared blowhards.

00:35:07.638 --> 00:35:10.163
I was looking for an excuse
to get away.

00:35:10.241 --> 00:35:12.903
You came back
because you cared about me,

00:35:12.977 --> 00:35:15.502
just like you care
about the Mark-1.

00:35:15.580 --> 00:35:18.276
You just won't admit it.

00:35:18.349 --> 00:35:19.509
He may not be perfect,

00:35:19.584 --> 00:35:21.575
but he's still one
of your creations,

00:35:21.652 --> 00:35:24.678
and right now,
he needs his creator.

00:35:24.755 --> 00:35:27.189
Don't turn your back on him.

00:35:43.474 --> 00:35:45.465
Computer,
activate Voyager's EMH.

00:35:45.543 --> 00:35:48.512
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:35:48.579 --> 00:35:49.511
You're the emergency.

00:35:49.580 --> 00:35:52.378
Where's Lieutenant Barclay?

00:35:52.450 --> 00:35:55.214
Trust me, you're in
far more capable hands.

00:35:55.286 --> 00:35:57.083
You're going
to repair my program?

00:35:57.155 --> 00:35:58.747
Who better?

00:35:58.823 --> 00:36:01.348
Just yesterday,
you threatened to decompile me.

00:36:01.425 --> 00:36:04.690
That was before your colleagues
made me feel guilty.

00:36:04.762 --> 00:36:06.252
You're ill.
You're in no condition

00:36:06.330 --> 00:36:08.195
to perform delicate procedures.

00:36:08.266 --> 00:36:09.460
I'll survive, but you won't

00:36:09.534 --> 00:36:11.365
if you don't relax
and let me finish.

00:36:12.937 --> 00:36:13.904
What are you doing?

00:36:13.971 --> 00:36:14.903
My scans identified

00:36:15.006 --> 00:36:17.338
a recursive error
in your pattern buffer.

00:36:17.408 --> 00:36:19.000
I'm trying to isolate it.

00:36:19.076 --> 00:36:21.670
Is that a fractal algorithm?

00:36:21.746 --> 00:36:23.008
Very good.

00:36:23.080 --> 00:36:25.571
I'm using it
to realign your matrix.

00:36:25.650 --> 00:36:28.312
Fractal algorithms are
notoriously unstable.

00:36:28.386 --> 00:36:30.251
In the hands of a novice.

00:36:30.321 --> 00:36:31.583
Whoops.

00:36:31.656 --> 00:36:33.647
"Whoops"? What's "whoops"?

00:36:34.859 --> 00:36:36.053
Computer, deactivate EMH.

00:36:36.127 --> 00:36:37.424
Ah...

00:36:48.372 --> 00:36:51.569
I-I... I can't move.

00:36:51.642 --> 00:36:52.802
I know.

00:36:52.877 --> 00:36:55.345
I had to take your
mobility subroutines

00:36:55.413 --> 00:36:56.778
off-line.

00:36:56.847 --> 00:36:58.439
How long have I
been deactivated?

00:36:58.516 --> 00:36:59.983
17 hours.

00:37:01.752 --> 00:37:04.346
I'm resetting your parameters.

00:37:06.057 --> 00:37:07.081
You don't look well.

00:37:08.192 --> 00:37:09.124
You need rest.

00:37:09.193 --> 00:37:10.125
I'm fine,

00:37:10.194 --> 00:37:11.252
and so are you.

00:37:11.329 --> 00:37:13.593
Your program's been stabilized.

00:37:13.664 --> 00:37:15.689
I... I'm going to be okay?

00:37:15.766 --> 00:37:17.597
No, you're going to be
better than okay.

00:37:17.668 --> 00:37:20.159
Now what are you doing?

00:37:21.239 --> 00:37:22.866
Welcome to Sick Bay.

00:37:22.940 --> 00:37:25.067
How may I help you today?

00:37:25.142 --> 00:37:26.336
Well, what do you think?

00:37:26.410 --> 00:37:28.241
I think you've altered
my greeting protocol.

00:37:28.312 --> 00:37:29.609
That's just the beginning.

00:37:29.680 --> 00:37:32.205
I've also added new subroutines

00:37:32.283 --> 00:37:35.912
for compassion, patience,
empathy, decorum.

00:37:35.987 --> 00:37:37.852
I don't feel any different.

00:37:37.922 --> 00:37:39.890
Because I haven't
installed them yet.

00:37:39.957 --> 00:37:42.790
I thought you'd like
to be awake for the big moment.

00:37:46.097 --> 00:37:48.122
Reginald was right about you.

00:37:48.199 --> 00:37:51.225
You have exceeded the
sum of your programming.

00:37:51.302 --> 00:37:52.496
You've accomplished

00:37:52.570 --> 00:37:55.300
far more than I would
have ever predicted.

00:37:55.373 --> 00:37:57.068
But let's face facts.

00:37:57.141 --> 00:38:00.110
You never overcame
the inherent flaws

00:38:00.177 --> 00:38:01.974
in your personality subroutines.

00:38:02.046 --> 00:38:04.776
You're arrogant, irritable...

00:38:04.849 --> 00:38:07.181
"a jerk," as Counselor
Troi would say.

00:38:07.251 --> 00:38:09.776
I believe she was
describing you, as well.

00:38:09.854 --> 00:38:11.344
Don't change the subject.

00:38:11.422 --> 00:38:12.446
I may not be able

00:38:12.523 --> 00:38:14.252
to turn you into a Mark-4,

00:38:14.325 --> 00:38:17.192
but I can make you
a bit more presentable.

00:38:17.261 --> 00:38:19.161
What if I'm happy
with the way I am?

00:38:19.230 --> 00:38:20.424
I'm doing you a favor.

00:38:20.498 --> 00:38:21.829
I don't want any favors,

00:38:21.899 --> 00:38:23.992
and I don't want
your new subroutines!

00:38:24.068 --> 00:38:25.899
Why can't you accept me
as I am?!

00:38:25.970 --> 00:38:28.097
Because you're defective!

00:38:30.041 --> 00:38:33.568
"Emergency Medical Hotheads!"

00:38:33.644 --> 00:38:36.772
"Extremely Marginal
House Calls."

00:38:36.847 --> 00:38:38.838
That's what everyone used
to call the Mark-1's,

00:38:38.916 --> 00:38:41.077
until they were bounced
out of the Medical Corps.

00:38:44.288 --> 00:38:46.153
I tried to have them
decommissioned,

00:38:46.223 --> 00:38:47.155
but Starfleet,

00:38:47.224 --> 00:38:49.055
in its infinite wisdom,
overruled me

00:38:49.126 --> 00:38:51.151
and reassigned them all to work

00:38:51.228 --> 00:38:53.856
waste-transfer barges.

00:38:57.101 --> 00:38:58.398
That's where you'd be, too,

00:38:58.469 --> 00:38:59.936
if you hadn't been lost

00:39:00.004 --> 00:39:01.437
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:39:10.715 --> 00:39:13.309
Do you know
how humiliating it is

00:39:13.384 --> 00:39:17.878
to have 675 Mark-1's out there

00:39:17.988 --> 00:39:20.980
scrubbing plasma conduits...

00:39:21.058 --> 00:39:24.892
all with my face?

00:39:27.698 --> 00:39:31.031
I'm sure
they're doing a fine job.

00:39:31.168 --> 00:39:32.135
What are you doing?

00:39:32.203 --> 00:39:33.636
I'm not finished with you.

00:39:33.704 --> 00:39:35.001
I'm trying to do my job.

00:39:35.072 --> 00:39:36.232
And if you give me a chance,

00:39:36.307 --> 00:39:37.865
you'll see
that I'm pretty good at it.

00:39:41.879 --> 00:39:46.316
Frankly, I'd hoped
that if we ever met,

00:39:46.384 --> 00:39:47.976
you'd be proud of me.

00:39:49.754 --> 00:39:51.312
Well...

00:39:51.389 --> 00:39:56.156
I guess it is comforting to know
that at least one of you

00:39:56.227 --> 00:39:59.321
is still doing
what I designed you to do.

00:40:01.365 --> 00:40:05.495
Your intercellular proteins
are at a dangerous level.

00:40:05.569 --> 00:40:09.266
We should begin the procedure.

00:40:09.340 --> 00:40:11.171
Please?

00:40:11.242 --> 00:40:14.643
Give me a chance
to make you proud of me.

00:40:21.318 --> 00:40:26.278
Maybe we could try it;
see how it goes.

00:40:27.324 --> 00:40:29.588
See how it goes.

00:40:29.660 --> 00:40:32.925
Just don't expect me
to put you in my will.

00:40:43.107 --> 00:40:44.131
I-I'm going in.

00:40:44.208 --> 00:40:45.232
Reg...

00:40:45.309 --> 00:40:47.675
They have been in
there for 32 hours!

00:40:47.745 --> 00:40:49.269
Be patient.

00:40:52.683 --> 00:40:53.980
Well, you...

00:40:54.118 --> 00:40:55.745
You're not fritzing anymore.

00:40:55.820 --> 00:40:57.151
No thanks to you.

00:40:57.221 --> 00:40:58.654
Dr. Zimmerman ran

00:40:58.722 --> 00:41:00.747
a diagnostic
on my subtronic relays,

00:41:00.825 --> 00:41:03.191
and he made
a very interesting discovery.

00:41:03.260 --> 00:41:06.320
Apparently, I was the victim

00:41:06.397 --> 00:41:07.921
of foul play.

00:41:08.032 --> 00:41:10.296
Well, what...
what do you mean?

00:41:10.367 --> 00:41:13.859
He found an algorithm
designed to disrupt

00:41:13.938 --> 00:41:15.371
my matrix.

00:41:15.439 --> 00:41:17.600
You wouldn't know
anything about that,

00:41:17.675 --> 00:41:19.370
would you?

00:41:19.443 --> 00:41:23.812
Well, traditional therapy
wasn't getting us anywhere.

00:41:23.881 --> 00:41:27.544
Well, your little scheme worked.

00:41:27.618 --> 00:41:29.347
Dr. Zimmerman has agreed

00:41:29.420 --> 00:41:31.445
to the cellular regeneration
procedure.

00:41:31.522 --> 00:41:33.422
It requires
several more treatments,

00:41:33.491 --> 00:41:35.982
but I'm optimistic
he'll make a full recovery.

00:41:48.772 --> 00:41:51.707
Trying to steal my secrets?

00:41:51.775 --> 00:41:54.608
Another one of my hobbies.

00:41:54.678 --> 00:41:58.273
I thought I'd take
home a few memories.

00:41:58.349 --> 00:41:59.577
You're supposed to be in bed.

00:41:59.650 --> 00:42:01.140
I've got work to do.

00:42:01.218 --> 00:42:02.150
It can wait.

00:42:02.219 --> 00:42:03.345
Go to bed.

00:42:03.420 --> 00:42:05.388
Doctor's orders.

00:42:06.557 --> 00:42:08.422
I hope you won't be
coming back next month

00:42:08.492 --> 00:42:10.119
to make sure
I'm taking my medicine.

00:42:10.194 --> 00:42:11.559
Don't worry.

00:42:11.629 --> 00:42:13.927
My Captain's not likely
to authorize another...

00:42:13.998 --> 00:42:15.761
house call.

00:42:15.833 --> 00:42:17.357
Good.

00:42:17.434 --> 00:42:20.892
The next time
she sends a data stream,

00:42:20.971 --> 00:42:25.203
you might want
to drop me a line,

00:42:25.276 --> 00:42:27.471
let me know how you're doing.

00:42:27.545 --> 00:42:29.979
If you insist.

00:42:37.788 --> 00:42:38.777
Ready?

00:42:49.099 --> 00:42:50.964
Would you mind?

00:42:51.101 --> 00:42:52.227
Not at all.

00:42:59.843 --> 00:43:01.333
Smile.
